          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Charles Darwin</strong><br>\nCharles Darwin was born on February 12, 1809, in Shrewsbury, England. As a child, Darwin showed a keen interest in nature and was fascinated by the diversity of life. He started medical studies at Edinburgh University but quickly realized that surgery was not his calling. Instead, he was drawn to natural history and spent a significant amount of time studying it.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Voyage of the HMS Beagle</strong><br>\nIn 1831, Darwin embarked on a voyage aboard the HMS Beagle as a naturalist. This trip around the world would take five years and have a profound impact on his thinking. Darwin collected a variety of natural specimens, including birds, plants, and fossils, and observed a rich variety of geological features.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Development of Evolutionary Thoughts</strong><br>\nDarwin's observations and collections from the Beagle voyage led him to question the origin of species. The diverse life forms of the Galapagos Islands were particularly influential. He noticed that each island had its own form of finch, which differed from one island to another, leading him to ponder the adaptation of species to their environments.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
