          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Origin of Species</strong><br>\nAfter years of meticulous research and thinking, Darwin published \"On the Origin of Species\" in 1859. His book proposed the theory of evolution by natural selection, explaining how species adapt and change over time. The book was both controversial and groundbreaking, altering the course of biological sciences.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Controversy and Acceptance</strong><br>\nDarwin's theory challenged the established scientific and religious beliefs of his time. Many people were skeptical or outright opposed to his ideas. Over time, however, as the evidence accumulated, the scientific community began to accept evolution as a fundamental principle of biology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Life and Research</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Darwin continued to write and publish on various biological topics, including human evolution and sexual selection. He maintained a vast correspondence with scientists around the world, enhancing his studies with a broad range of insights.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
