            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Impact on Science and Society</strong><br>\nDarwin's work laid the foundation for the field of evolutionary biology. His ideas also had significant social and philosophical implications, influencing a range of disciplines from psychology to anthropology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Charles Darwin</strong><br>\nDarwin's legacy is seen in the acceptance of evolution as a central concept in biology. His birthday, February 12, is celebrated by scientists worldwide as \"Darwin Day.\" His home at Down House in Kent has been preserved as a museum dedicated to his life and work.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Reflections on Darwin</strong><br>\nEven after his death in 1882, Darwin's influence continues. His theory remains a topic of discussion and development within science. Darwin's ability to think broadly and integrate observations into a coherent theory exemplifies the scientific method and the pursuit of knowledge.</p>\n"
              },
